{
  "summary": "Escapes backslashes in the Tor control port `AUTHENTICATE` command when using `HASHEDPASSWORD` authentication. Also adds functional test coverage with a mock Tor control server verifying backslash and quote escaping.",
  "problem": "Bitcoin Core sends `AUTHENTICATE \"<password>\"` under `HASHEDPASSWORD` authentication but only escapes double quotes. Tor treats backslashes in quoted strings as escape characters according to the control specification, causing passwords containing backslashes to be corrupted or malform the command syntax, which fails authentication and prevents onion service creation.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Tested against Tor 0.4.9.12 with HashedControlPassword set for pa\\ss\"word\\: on master bitcoind logs \"tor: Authentication failed\", with this change authentication succeeds and ADD_ONION creates the onion service.'",
    "PR description notes that with '-torpassword=pa\\ss\"word\\', master sends 'AUTHENTICATE \"pa\\ss\\\"word\\\"' whereas the fix sends 'AUTHENTICATE \"pa\\\\ss\\\"word\\\\\"'."
  ],
